@startuml
title SEQ-01 - Registration, Login and OAuth
autonumber
actor User
boundary Client as "Web / Chrome"
control Core
database CoreDB as "PostgreSQL core"
participant OAuth as "Google / Facebook"

User -> Client: Choose email/password or OAuth
alt Email registration
  Client -> Core: POST /auth/register\nX-Application-Key: gotit\n{email,password}
  Core -> CoreDB: Resolve active application
  Core -> CoreDB: Find user by application + normalized email
  break Existing identity cannot register
    Core --> Client: 409 USER_ALREADY_EXISTS
  end
  Core -> Core: Argon2id hash password
  critical Atomic account creation
    Core -> CoreDB: Insert application_user
    Core -> CoreDB: Insert password_credential
    Core -> CoreDB: Insert auth_session(refresh hash)
  end
else Email login
  Client -> Core: POST /auth/login\n{email,password}
  Core -> CoreDB: Load scoped credential/user
  Core -> Core: Verify Argon2id
  break Missing/wrong/disabled
    Core --> Client: 401 INVALID_CREDENTIALS or USER_DISABLED
  end
  Core -> CoreDB: Insert auth_session(refresh hash)
else OAuth
  Client -> OAuth: Interactive provider flow
  OAuth --> Client: ID token or user access token
  Client -> Core: POST /auth/google|facebook
  Core -> CoreDB: Load provider client for application
  Core -> OAuth: Verify token, audience/app, expiry, email
  OAuth --> Core: verified subject + verified email
  critical Resolve identity
    Core -> CoreDB: Reuse provider subject OR link verified email OR create user
    Core -> CoreDB: Insert/update oauth_identity + session
  end
end
Core -> Core: Sign short-lived JWT\nformat rotating refresh token
Core --> Client: user + accessToken + refreshToken + expiresIn
Client -> Client: Access in memory/session\nRefresh in approved storage
Client --> User: Authenticated application
note over Core,CoreDB
No global user. Email and provider identity are scoped by application.
Role is loaded from DB, never accepted from registration input.
end note
@enduml

